# Scope Guardrails

Follow `AGENTS.md` and the approved docs in `docs/`. Do not invent requirements, sources, endpoints, weights, or tables.

## Stage

Documentation is approved. Implement a phase only when `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` says it is in scope and the user has asked for that phase. Finish its manual checks before the next phase.

Must-have beats should-have beats nice-to-have. Cut in the order that plan lists. Do not drop evidence, the rules score, or insufficient-evidence behavior.

## Stack

React, Vite, Tailwind, Zustand, TanStack Query, Recharts, `lucide-react`, Clerk on the frontend. FastAPI, Supabase PostgreSQL, pgvector, LangChain where the AI design allows it, Requests, BeautifulSoup, APScheduler on the backend.

Do not add a dependency, queue, cache, or service that `docs/TECHNICAL_PRD.md` does not name. Clerk, `lucide-react`, React Router, and PyJWT (Clerk token verification only) are already approved.

## Simplicity

One backend process. No Kafka, Celery, Redis, Kubernetes, or microservices. No extra abstraction "for later". No premature optimization. Exact vector search is enough until the design says otherwise.

Do not create test files unless the user explicitly asks.
